  = must: preserve existing duty identities and lineage when refreshing contracts
  = must: prevent generic operator runner or packetization contracts from hiding dispatch, operations-control, or live-control authority

& [P3OperatorRefreshGapLedger] is the gap ledger produced by P3-S01
  + [refresh_gap] is common operator envelope must expose P2 authority_class, effect_boundary, currentness_state, review_gate_ref, invalidation_ref_set, natural_key_state, source_ref_set, and lineage_edge_set as explicit contract terms
  + [refresh_gap] is SOP-first interrupt semantics must distinguish semantic ambiguity, authority conflict, stale input, high-risk operation, missing proof route, and human override without hiding fault output
  + [refresh_gap] is output mutation policy must preserve create_new_record, supersede_existing_record, append_lineage_edge, append_review, and no_hidden_write behavior
  + [refresh_gap] is signature_validation must be refreshed against satisfaction signature protocol, source manifest hashes, wrong protocol, stale source hash, duplicate signatures, broken lineage, and ambiguous identity
  + [refresh_gap] is support_readiness_recompute must be refreshed against P2 support gaps, requirement deltas, stale projections, contradicted support, missing proof route, authority conflict, hidden authority, and false-ready prevention
  + [refresh_gap] is planning_readiness_recompute must be reconciled with support_readiness_recompute to prevent duplicate or contradictory readiness operators
  + [refresh_gap] is operator trace schema must distinguish proof output, generated output, projection output, checkpoint state, carrier context, blocked output, fault output, and SOP-first interrupt context
  + [refresh_gap] is fixture oracle remains plan-only and must not create fixture source files or expected ledgers
  + [refresh_gap] is no-automation boundary must prevent operator contract acceptance from becoming implementation, graph node execution, dispatch, operations-control, or live-control authority

  = must: resolve or explicitly defer these gaps in P3-S02 through P3-S05
  = must: prevent any gap from silently becoming downstream support

& [SupersessionPosture: P3-S01] is the supersession posture for existing operator authority
  + [Operator_Contract_Template.v1.sop] is accepted_boundary_input_not_superseded
  + [Foundation_Operator_Contracts.v1.sop] is accepted_boundary_input_not_superseded
  + [Planning_Readiness_Operator_Contracts.v1.sop] is accepted_boundary_input_not_superseded
  + [IR3_Contract_Driven_Operator_Runner_And_Trace_Contract.v1.sop] is accepted_boundary_input_not_superseded
  + [next_possible_supersession_slice] is P3-S02 for common operator envelope and refusal semantics
  + [next_possible_supersession_slice] is P3-S03 for signature validation operator contract
  + [next_possible_supersession_slice] is P3-S04 for support readiness recompute operator contract
  + [implementation_supersession_authorized] is false
  + [runtime_supersession_authorized] is false

  = must: preserve current operator authority for existing proof packs until refreshed and accepted
  = must: mark downstream consumers stale if a later P3 slice supersedes an operator input

